### `FoodController.java`

This controller has two POST methods and one GET method. No service class and no repository code are needed.

```java
package com.example.foodapp.controller;

import com.example.foodapp.model.*;
import com.example.foodapp.repository.*;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import java.util.*;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api")
@CrossOrigin(origins = "http://localhost:5173")
public class FoodController {

    @Autowired
    FoodOrderRepository foodRepository;

    @Autowired
    CustomerRepository customerRepository;

    // Add food order
    @PostMapping("/foodorders")
    public FoodOrder addFood(@RequestBody FoodOrder f) {
        return foodRepository.save(f);
    }

    // Add customer
    @PostMapping("/customers")
    public Customer addCustomer(@RequestBody Customer c) {
        return customerRepository.save(c);
    }

    // Get customers who chose veg food
    @GetMapping("/vegcustomers")
    public List<Customer> getVegCustomers() {

        List<FoodOrder> foods = foodRepository.findAll();
        List<Customer> customers = customerRepository.findAll();
        List<Customer> result = new ArrayList<>();

        for (FoodOrder f : foods) {
            if (f.getCat() != null &&
                f.getCat().equalsIgnoreCase("veg")) {

                for (Customer c : customers) {
                    if (c.getCustid().equals(f.getCustid()) &&
                        !result.contains(c)) {
                        result.add(c);
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

### `application.properties`

```properties
spring.application.name=Foodapp
spring.mongodb.uri=mongodb://localhost:27017/test
server.port=8080
```

The database is `test`. MongoDB creates the `foodorders` and `customer` collections when records are saved.

### 2\. Postman APIs

Run your Spring Boot application first.

### API 1 — Add a food order

`http://localhost:8080/api/foodorders`

Body → raw → JSON:

```json
{
  "foodid": "F1",
  "custid": "C101",
  "name": "Paneer Rice",
  "price": 150,
  "cat": "veg"
}
```

Add another food order:

```json
{
  "foodid": "F2",
