  "name": "Chicken Rice",
  "price": 200,
  "cat": "nonveg"
}
```

### API 2 — Add a customer

`http://localhost:8080/api/customers`

Body → raw → JSON:

```json
{
  "custid": "C101",
  "name": "Arun"
}
```

Add another customer:

```json
{
  "custid": "C102",
  "name": "Priya"
}
```

### API 3 — Get all customers who chose veg

`http://localhost:8080/api/vegcustomers`

Expected response:

```json
[
  {
    "custid": "C101",
    "name": "Arun"
  }
]
```

The GET method matches `custid` between both collections and returns only customers with at least one veg order.

### 3\. Frontend — Vue.js

Replace your `src/App.vue` with this simple code. No component, no table, and no `index.html` changes are needed.

```vue
<script setup>
import { ref, onMounted } from 'vue'

const customers = ref([])
const foodid = ref(''), custid = ref('')
const name = ref(''), price = ref('')
const cat = ref('')
const cid = ref(''), cname = ref('')
const page = ref('home')

const foodApi = 'http://localhost:8080/api/foodorders'
const custApi = 'http://localhost:8080/api/customers'
const vegApi = 'http://localhost:8080/api/vegcustomers'

async function getVeg() {
  customers.value = await (await fetch(vegApi)).json()
}

async function saveFood() {
  await fetch(foodApi, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      foodid: foodid.value,
      custid: custid.value,
      name: name.value,
      price: Number(price.value),
      cat: cat.value
    })
  })

  alert('Food order saved')
  foodid.value = custid.value = name.value = price.value = cat.value = ''
}

async function saveCustomer() {
  await fetch(custApi, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      custid: cid.value,
      name: cname.value
    })
  })

  alert('Customer saved')
  cid.value = cname.value = ''
}

onMounted(getVeg)
</script>

<template>
  <h1>Food Order Management</h1>

  <a href="#" @click.prevent="page='home'">Home</a> |
  <a href="#" @click.prevent="page='food'">Add Food</a> |
  <a href="#" @click.prevent="page='customer'">Add Customer</a> |
  <a href="#" @click.prevent="page='veg'; getVeg()">Veg Customers</a>

  <hr>

  <div v-if="page==='home'">
    <h2>Welcome</h2>
  </div>

  <div v-if="page==='food'">
    <h2>Add Food Order</h2>
    <input v-model="foodid" placeholder="Food ID">
    <input v-model="custid" placeholder="Customer ID">
    <input v-model="name" placeholder="Food Name">
    <input v-model="price" type="number" placeholder="Price">
    <input v-model="cat" placeholder="veg or nonveg">
    <button @click="saveFood">Save Food</button>
  </div>

  <div v-if="page==='customer'">
    <h2>Add Customer</h2>
    <input v-model="cid" placeholder="Customer ID">
    <input v-model="cname" placeholder="Customer Name">
    <button @click="saveCustomer">Save Customer</button>
  </div>

  <div v-if="page==='veg'">
    <h2>Customers Who Chose Veg</h2>
    <button @click="getVeg">Refresh</button>
    <p v-for="c in customers" :key="c.custid">
      {{ c.custid }} - {{ c.name }}
    </p>
    <p v-if="customers.length===0">No veg customers found</p>
  </div>
</template>
```

### 4\. Test in this order

* Start MongoDB and Spring Boot.

* Run Vue using `npm run dev`.

* Add a customer with ID `C101`.

* Add a food order with customer ID `C101` and category `veg`.

* Click Veg Customers.

You should see `C101 - Arun`.

Exam tip: Remember the pattern: two model classes → two repositories → one controller with two POST methods and one GET method → Vue uses `fetch()` to call each API.
